EXT. ICE FIELD - LATE AFTERNOON

White. Everywhere. Wind drags spindrift across the surface like smoke.

A tiny orange tent, half-collapsed. Skis stabbed upright in the snow.

TOVE HALVORSEN (30s, frostbitten cheeks, goggles pushed up, a pack nearly as big as she is) crawls out of the tent on hands and knees.

She stands. Staggers. Catches herself on a ski.

A handheld radio hangs from her chest strap. She thumbs it.

TOVE
Base, this is Tove. Do you copy?

Static.

TOVE (CONT'D)
Base. Tove. Anyone.

Static. A hiss. Then, far away, thin as wire:

BASE CAMP (V.O.)
(over radio)
...ove... copy... say position...

TOVE
Seventy-nine north. Three kilometers past the cairn.

BASE CAMP (V.O.)
...repeat...

TOVE
Past the cairn! I've lost one ski pole! Tent's torn!

BASE CAMP (V.O.)
...storm... front... twelve hours...

She looks up. To the west: a bruise-colored wall of cloud, creeping.

TOVE
Twelve hours. Okay.

She drops to her knees. Digs in her pack. Pulls out a thermos, shakes it, unscrews the cap. Drinks. Grimaces. Frozen slush.

She tosses it. It skitters across the ice.

Wind picks up. The tent flaps. The first flakes begin to fall.

TOVE (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Pack. Move. Pack. Move.

She grabs the tent poles. They snap in her gloves. She stares at the splinters.

BASE CAMP (V.O.)
...Tove... turn... back...

TOVE
There is no back!

She keys the radio again, voice cracking.

TOVE (CONT'D)
Base, I'm going to walk. East. Toward the lights.

BASE CAMP (V.O.)
...no lights... east...

She stops. Looks east. Nothing but white.

The snow thickens. She zips her jacket to her chin. Lifts the pack. Staggers one step. Two.

Behind her, the tent collapses completely.
